  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Fei He mountain, Immortal Crane Sect holds a middle examination in its sparring arena, and Fang Zheng becomes an elite disciple after defeating Sun Yuan Hua.",
      "chapters": [
        334
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-crane-at-fei-he",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_fei_he_mountain",
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
        "char_fang_zheng",
        "char_sun_yuan_hua"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Before the flight toward Tian Ti, Immortal Crane elites are told the lord Gu Immortals have agreed not to strike and will send elite disciples to compete fairly for Gu Immortal Bai Hu’s inheritance instead. The same briefing names Heavenly Lotus Sect, Spirit Butterfly Valley, Ancient Soul Sect, Heaven’s Envy Sect, and the other Central Continent top ten sects as co-competitors, and says Immortal Crane Sect must stay united on the trip.",
      "chapters": [
        335
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "hu-immortal-contest-briefing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_tian_ti",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_fairy_bai_hu",
        "fac_heavenly_lotus_sect",
        "loc_spirit_butterfly_valley",
        "fac_ancient_soul_sect",
        "fac_heavens_envy_sect",
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On the road toward Tian Ti, Fang Zheng tells fellow Immortal Crane elites that the contestants for that inheritance are all elites from the ten great sects, and that among those sects each has deep foundations and talented people. Demonic attackers fleeing the crane charge likewise identify Immortal Crane’s elite disciples as belonging to one of the ten great sects.",
      "chapters": [
        336
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "recognition-as-sect-elites",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Several months before the inheritance climb, the ten great sects send an order at the same time to organize a great competition for elite disciples and determine rankings. Elite disciples from the ten great sects gather at the foot of Tian Ti for that climb. Gu Immortal talk at the mountain names Spirit Butterfly Valley’s Xiao Qi Xing and Myriad Dragon Dock’s Ying Sheng Ji among the outstanding juniors of that generation.",
      "chapters": [
        365
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "disciple-ranking-at-tian-ti",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_xiao_qi_xing",
        "fac_myriad_dragon_dock",
        "char_ying_sheng_ji"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration later calls the ten great sects the heads of Central Continent and says even Southern Border’s top clans cannot compare to them. In that generation’s ranking talk, disciples such as Fang Zheng, Fairy Bi Xia, Gu Ting, and Wei Wu Shang sit only in the second tier, while the first tier includes Feng Jin Huang of Spirit Affinity House, Ying Sheng Ji, and Xiao Qi Xing. The same stretch treats the Hu Immortal Inheritance contest as a battle between the ten great sects, with disciples as chess pieces and the Gu Immortals of the ten sects as the players behind the scenes.",
      "chapters": [
        366
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "disciple-ranking-at-tian-ti",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "char_fairy_bi_xia",
        "char_gu_ting",
        "char_wei_wu_shang",
        "char_feng_jin_huang",
        "fac_spirit_affinity_house",
        "inh_hu_immortal_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Black Heaven Temple is called one of the ten great ancient sects when Central Continent Gu Immortals argue over reputation while hunting in Northern Plains.",
      "chapters": [
        811
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-member-sects",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_black_heaven_temple",
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wind Cloud Manor is likewise named as one of the ten when Hong Chi Ming’s Gu formation background is explained.",
      "chapters": [
        923
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-member-sects",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_wind_cloud_manor",
        "char_hong_chi_ming",
        "sys_gu_formation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Combat Immortal Sect states the same membership when explaining its disciple selection rules.",
      "chapters": [
        1227
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-member-sects",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_combat_immortal_sect"
      ]
    }
  ],
